{"availability":"available","full":"Klotzkette/isometric-berlin","name":"isometric-berlin","description":"Open-data 3D isometric viewer of Berlin's Regierungsviertel, built from official Berlin 3D mesh/LoD2, OSM, and documented civic detail.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-06-14T13:51:08Z","updated":"2026-10-10T14:59:23Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://klotzkette.github.io/isometric-berlin/","topics":[],"demo":"https://klotzkette.github.io/isometric-berlin/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T15:05:56.409Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T15:05:56.409Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T15:05:56.409Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T15:05:56.409Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The downloadable viewer is the built React + Three.js app from src/app/. It always presents the isometric 3D city, in Day, Night, Snowstorm, Minecraft, Schwellenraum or Flooded Berlin, on modern desktop, phone and tablet browsers. No AI model, Google key or paid service is needed at runtime. GitHub Pages and the release ZIP use the same viewer and all required local assets.","For local use, extract the whole ZIP and launch OPEN-3D-WINDOWS.bat on Windows, OPEN-3D-MAC.command on macOS, or sh start-linux.sh on Linux. Alternatively, run python3 serve-local.py in the extracted folder. Python 3 is required. START-HERE.html shows these instructions when double-clicked; when served over HTTP, it opens the same 3D viewer. See Run locally.","Status: Public open-data project · Local v1.0.112 · static viewer and a complete local package for macOS, Windows, and Linux."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Klotzkette/isometric-berlin/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"c71079a29a8125397fc23940e8cf03038fd8061cdd0729310e7d7fbe082db51e","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T15:05:56.613Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T15:05:56.613Z","projectInsights":{"version":1